    "readout_answer": "-1",
    "readout_text": "To determine the value of $ a_{2023} $ in the given identity:\n\n$$\n\\tan(2023x) = \\frac{a_1 \\tan x + a_3 \\tan^3 x + a_5 \\tan^5 x + \\cdots + a_{2023} \\tan^{2023} x}{1 + a_2 \\tan^2 x + a_4 \\tan^4 x + \\cdots + a_{2022} \\tan^{2022} x}\n$$\n\nwe recognize that this is a standard expansion of the tangent of a multiple angle. Specifically, the identity for $ \\tan(nx) $ in terms of $ \\tan x $ is well-known and can be expressed as:\n\n$$\n\\tan(nx) = \\frac{\\sum_{k=0}^{\\lfloor (n-1)/2 \\rfloor} (-1)^k \\binom{n}{2k+1} \\tan^{2k+1}x}{\\sum_{k=0}^{\\lfloor n/2 \\rfloor} (-1)^k \\binom{n}{2k} \\tan^{2k}x}\n$$\n\nThis formula is valid for all integers $ n $, and it separates the expression into a numerator with only odd powers of $ \\tan x $ and a denominator with only even powers of $ \\tan x $, which matches the structure of the given problem.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Identify the Coefficient $ a_{2023} $\n\nIn the numerator of the given expression, the general term is:\n\n$$\na_{2m+1} \\tan^{2m+1}x\n$$\n\nWe are asked to find $ a_{2023} $, which corresponds to the coefficient of $ \\tan^{2023}x $ in the numerator. This occurs when $ 2m+1 = 2023 $, so:\n\n$$\nm = \\frac{2023 - 1}{2} = 1011\n$$\n\nThus, the coefficient $ a_{2023} $ is given by:\n\n$$\na_{2023} = (-1)^{1011} \\binom{2023}{2023}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Evaluate the Expression\n\n- $ \\binom{2023}{2023} = 1 $\n- $ (-1)^{1011} = -1 $, since 1011 is odd\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\na_{2023} = -1\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{-1}\n$$",
